# Copy to .env and edit. Every value below is the default.

# Host port. 8927 rather than 8000, which is already taken on most home servers.
PORT=8927

# Single volume holding the database, media and the instance secret.
# Back up the whole thing: tar czf backup.tgz /data
DATA_DIR=/data

# builtin  - accounts live here; the first start opens a setup wizard
# proxy    - identity comes from a reverse proxy (Authelia, authentik, ...)
# disabled - no authentication at all; only sane on a trusted localhost
AUTH_MODE=builtin
PROXY_USER_HEADER=X-Remote-User

# Usernames that are administrators whatever the database says, comma
# separated. Required with AUTH_MODE=proxy, where every identity arrives
# without the flag and nobody could otherwise configure the instance. In
# builtin mode it is the way back in if the only password is lost.
# ADMIN_USERS=alice,bob

# How long a signed session cookie stays valid.
SESSION_MAX_AGE_DAYS=30

# Set to true once the instance is served over HTTPS, so the session cookie
# never travels in the clear. Leave false while testing over plain http.
SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE=false

# Largest upload accepted, in bytes. Default is 5 GiB. The same limit applies to
# anything fetched from a link, counted as the bytes arrive.
MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE=5368709120

# --- Links --------------------------------------------------------------
# A link ending in a media extension is streamed straight from the server;
# anything else is a page, and a page goes to yt-dlp, which knows ~1800 sites.
#
# How long to wait for the far end to answer. The body itself has no deadline:
# a two-hour recording takes as long as it takes.
DOWNLOAD_CONNECT_SECONDS=30

# Links resolving to a private, loopback or link-local address are refused, so
# that an account here cannot be used to read the cloud metadata endpoint or
# find out which ports on the host answer. Turn this on if the whole point of
# your instance is pulling recordings off a NAS on the same LAN.
ALLOW_PRIVATE_NETWORK_URLS=false

# The extractor is a binary, not a library, because it releases far more often
# than this app does. Point this at a newer one to update without a rebuild.
YTDLP_BIN=yt-dlp

# --- Speech to text -----------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible /v1/audio/transcriptions endpoint: speaches, whisper.cpp
# server, faster-whisper-server, LocalAI, or the OpenAI API itself.
#
# These three seed the database on an empty installation and are ignored
# afterwards -- from then on the provider is edited in the app, not here.
#
# Reaching a service on the host from inside the container needs
# host.docker.internal, not localhost. That mistake accounts for most
# self-hosting failures, and the app's connection test exists to catch it.
STT_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8000/v1
STT_MODEL=Systran/faster-whisper-small
# STT_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Summaries ----------------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions endpoint: Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM,
# OpenWebUI, or a cloud API. Leave unset and transcription still works; only
# summarising is unavailable.
LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
LLM_MODEL=qwen3:8b
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-...

# The context window of the model above. Deliberately low by default: guessing
# too high is the dangerous direction, because Ollama silently truncates the
# input and returns a confident summary of the first third of the recording.
# Guessing too low only costs an unnecessary map-reduce pass.
LLM_CONTEXT_TOKENS=8192

# --- Chunking -----------------------------------------------------------
# Long recordings are cut at pauses, never at fixed intervals: a cut in the
# middle of a word makes Whisper hallucinate or lose the phrase across the
# seam, and the result still reads like prose, so nobody notices.
#
# auto   - split only when the recording is longer than the maximum below
# always - split everything
# never  - send whole files, whatever their length
STT_CHUNKING=auto
CHUNK_TARGET_SECONDS=600
CHUNK_MAX_SECONDS=900

# Retries apply to one chunk, not the whole recording, and only to failures
# that look like transport: a refused connection, a timeout, a 5xx. A 4xx means
# the request itself is wrong, so it fails immediately.
STT_RETRY_ATTEMPTS=3
STT_RETRY_BACKOFF_SECONDS=2

# --- Diarisation --------------------------------------------------------
# Who spoke when. There is no OpenAI-compatible endpoint for this, so it is a
# service with a contract of its own: POST /diarize, get turns back. Leave it
# unset and the option is not offered at all, which is better than a checkbox
# that fails twenty minutes into a job.
#
#   docker compose --profile diarize up -d
#
# DIARIZER_URL=http://diarizer:9000
#
# Read by the diarizer container, not by the app. The model is gated: accept the
# terms of pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1 once on huggingface.co with the same
# account, then put a read token here or the download answers 403.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...

# --- Automation ---------------------------------------------------------
# Every finished job is POSTed here as JSON: the job, and the text if it
# succeeded. One attempt, no retries and no queue -- this is a courtesy call,
# and the API is still there to be polled. Leave unset to send nothing.
# WEBHOOK_URL=http://n8n.internal:5678/webhook/tany
# Sent as "Authorization: Bearer ...", so the receiver can tell it is us.
# WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Worker -------------------------------------------------------------
# How long a job may go without a heartbeat before a restarting worker decides
# its predecessor died and puts it back in the queue.
HEARTBEAT_STALE_SECONDS=120
